  grid: 10-30 rows x 13-30 cols
  background: single dominant color (any color 0-9)
  legend:
    shape: 2 columns wide, 3-7 rows tall, fully filled (no bg cells)
    distinct_colors: >=3 (required by solver)
    separation: no non-bg pixel 8-adjacent to the legend
    position: anywhere in grid [observed: near corner or interior]
    each_row: (src_color, dst_color) substitution pair; src != dst per row
    chaining: a src color may appear as dst in an earlier row, enabling multi-step rewrites
    repeated_src: same color may appear as src in multiple rows [observed in test]
    no_identity: after applying full chain top-to-bottom, no src color maps back to itself
  targets:
    description: non-bg pixels outside the legend; mix of scattered single pixels and/or multi-pixel monochromatic objects
    count: 3-131 target pixels total; 1-10 distinct colors
    some_match_src: a subset of target colors match legend src colors and get rewritten
    some_unchanged: >=1 target color not in any legend src column stays unchanged
    divider: 0-1 full-spanning line (row or column) of a single non-bg, non-src color; when present it separates the legend/table side from the scattered-object side
    multi_step_targets: common; many changed target pixels require following 2-3 legend rows before reaching their final color
  output: legend and bg unchanged; each target pixel's color is run through the legend chain top-to-bottom

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (transform is simple recolor, no geometric constraints)
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size, bg color
    2. Build legend pairs (3-7 rows); pick 5-8 distinct non-bg colors, assign (src, dst) pairs ensuring >=3 distinct colors in the 2xN block, no src maps to itself after full chain, and several src colors chain through 2-3 substitutions
    3. Place legend as a 2xN block isolated by >=1 bg cell from all other non-bg pixels
    4. Usually place a full-spanning divider line in a non-src, non-bg color between the legend/table region and the scattered-object region
    5. Scatter target objects (single pixels or small monochromatic blobs) on the opposite side of any divider; use a mix of src colors that include multi-step chain starts and non-src colors that stay unchanged
    6. Verify legend is the unique connected 2-col fully-filled component with >=3 colors
